    {
      "changed_at": "2026-10-08T15:00:23.712084+00:00",
      "first_week_applied": {
        "season": 2026,
        "week": 6
      },
      "score_week_git_commit": "95e41edaf3441f79835f28e6f0ff950451b56fe3",
      "note": "From 2026 week 6, model/score_week.py no longer scores a player whose team has no game that week (a bye): he is listed in no_game_watch_list instead of being ranked. Before this, bye-week players were ranked like everyone else and counted here as DNP misses. Weeks 1-4 had no byes, so they are the same either way. Week 5 is the one week affected: its first snapshot (predictions/2026_week05.json, generated 2026-10-08 before the change) is frozen WITH bye-week players in it (CAR and KC), and they are guaranteed misses for that week. Do not average week 5's precision with other weeks without accounting for that. The historical table the model was trained and evaluated on only ever held player-weeks that were played, so from week 6 the live pool matches it.",
      "week_5_first_snapshot_bye_players": {
        "production": {
          "top_10": 3,
          "top_25": 6
        },
        "shadow": {
          "top_10": 0,
          "top_25": 4
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "changed_at": "2026-10-15T21:26:08.236356+00:00",
      "first_week_applied": {
        "season": 2026,
        "week": 7
      },
      "score_week_git_commit": "91da696c17d5c275194211c9937da866e5df8573",
      "note": "From 2026 week 7, model/score_week.py no longer scores a player who is not on an NFL roster per nflverse's weekly roster (newest row at or before the week is CUT or RET, no row this season, or no row for the week although his team has rows): he is listed in off_roster_watch_list instead of being ranked. The exempt list (EXE) joined the availability gate at the same time. Before this, released and unsigned players were ranked on their stats-history team (found 2026-10-15: Andy Dalton, released by PHI in week 5, ranked #47 in week 6). Week 6's first snapshot (predictions/2026_week06.json, the thu run of 2026-10-15) was generated before the change and is frozen as logged; week 6's sun run (2026-10-18) is the first run under the check but is not what this log verifies. In week 6's first snapshot none of these players is in either model's top 25 (counts below), so its precision@10/@25 are unaffected. Weeks 1-5 are not re-examined here; the tracker's reports footnote weeks 4-6 (tracker/off_roster_audit_20261015.json).",
      "week_6_first_snapshot_off_roster_or_exempt_players": {
        "production": {
          "top_10": 0,
          "top_25": 0
        },
        "shadow": {
          "top_10": 0,
          "top_25": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "changed_at": "2026-10-18T15:25:46.968897+00:00",
      "first_week_applied": {
        "season": 2026,
        "week": 7
      },
      "score_week_git_commit": "b4cff44f19116a25741f4a92d9159e4f350b9665",
      "note": "From 2026 week 7, model/score_week.py no longer ranks a player designated Out or Doubtful on the week's NFL injury report when the snapshot is generated (tracker/injuries.py's rule, shared with the tracker's pool rule: nflverse's injuries release, ESPN's injuryStatus as the fallback; Questionable players stay in). He is listed in injury_watch_list instead. Before this, Out/Doubtful players were ranked and counted here as misses if they didn't play. Week 6's first snapshot (predictions/2026_week06.json, the thu run of 2026-10-15) was generated before the change and is frozen as logged; at its log time the report designated none of its pool players Out or Doubtful (a Thursday run only sees Thursday-game designations), so the check would not have changed it. What the check cannot know: Sunday teams' designations before Friday, and game-day inactives -- a thu snapshot will still rank players later ruled out.",
      "week_6_first_snapshot_out_doubtful_at_log_time": {
        "source": "nflverse",
        "excluded": 0
      }
    }
  ],
